# Plan Mode: Front-End Basic Template

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a basic planning template for front-end development in the PolygonExpress project. It is designed for planning straightforward components with minimal state and dependencies.

This file complements:
- **front-end-workflow.md**: Core front-end development workflow
- **dev-mode-front-end-log-based.md**: Implementation approach

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/plan-mode-front-end-basic.mdc
```

## Template Structure

When this template is applied, the planning folder will be structured as follows:

```
planning/
  ├── requirements.md (Initial requirements)
  ├── context-component.md (Component analysis)
  ├── implementation-component.md (Implementation approach)
  ├── test-cheatsheet.md (Testing scenarios)
  └── README.md (Overview)
```

## Planning Process

### 1. Requirements Analysis

The requirements.md file should document:

- Core component functionality
- User interaction patterns
- Visual design requirements
- Integration points with other components
- Success criteria

```markdown
# Requirements: [Component Name]

## Objective
[Clear statement of component purpose]

## Core Requirements
1. [Functional requirement 1]
2. [Functional requirement 2]
3. [Functional requirement 3]

## Technical Requirements
1. [Technical requirement 1]
2. [Technical requirement 2]

## Visual Requirements
1. [Visual requirement 1]
2. [Visual requirement 2]

## Success Criteria
- [Criterion 1]
- [Criterion 2]
- [Criterion 3]
```

### 2. Component Context Analysis

The context-component.md file should document:

- Related existing components
- State management approach
- Event handling patterns
- API interactions
- Rendering logic

```markdown
# Context Analysis: [Component Name]

## Related Components
- [Component 1]: [Relationship]
- [Component 2]: [Relationship]

## State Management
- [State variable 1]: [Purpose]
- [State variable 2]: [Purpose]

## Event Handling
- [Event 1]: [Handling approach]
- [Event 2]: [Handling approach]

## API Interactions
- [API endpoint 1]: [Interaction pattern]
- [API endpoint 2]: [Interaction pattern]

## Rendering Logic
- [Condition 1]: [Rendering outcome]
- [Condition 2]: [Rendering outcome]
```

### 3. Implementation Planning

The implementation-component.md file should document:

- Component structure
- Props interface
- Hook implementation
- Styling approach
- Testing strategy

```markdown
# Implementation Plan: [Component Name]

## Component Structure
```tsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

interface [Component]Props {
  // Props definition
}

export const [Component]: React.FC<[Component]Props> = ({ 
  // Props destructuring
}) => {
  // State hooks
  
  // Effect hooks
  
  // Event handlers
  
  // Render
  return (
    // JSX structure
  );
};
```

## Hooks Implementation
- `useState`: [Implementation details]
- `useEffect`: [Implementation details]
- `useCallback`: [Implementation details]

## Styling Approach
- [Styling technique]
- [Key style considerations]

## Testing Strategy
- [Test 1]: [Testing approach]
- [Test 2]: [Testing approach]
```

### 4. Testing Cheatsheet

The test-cheatsheet.md file should document:

- User interactions to test
- Expected behavior
- Edge cases
- Error scenarios

```markdown
# Test Cheatsheet: [Component Name]

## Basic Functionality Tests
- [Test scenario 1]
- [Test scenario 2]

## Edge Case Tests
- [Edge case 1]
- [Edge case 2]

## Error Handling Tests
- [Error scenario 1]
- [Error scenario 2]

## Performance Tests
- [Performance scenario 1]
- [Performance scenario 2]
```

## Planning Completion

When planning is complete, signal completion with:

```
📋 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]

planning-document-complete
```

## Implementation Transition

After planning completion, transition to implementation with:

```
dev-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/dev-mode/dev-mode-front-end-basic.mdc
``` 